From 5db4c2f122be6fe7dbe6bd06310065505b2c008d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chronium <chronium@interlink.local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:40:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronium: seeded WebGL readPixels noise + render-time audio
 noise

Engine Fix Notes A1: readPixels returned raw pixels and
noise.webgl_readpixels was never read.
- ReadPixelsHelper applies the same seeded "canvas" LSB mask as
  toDataURL/toBlob/getImageData, in canvas space (GL rows flipped), to
  RGBA/UNSIGNED_BYTE reads of the default framebuffer, so readPixels,
  toDataURL and drawImage+getImageData agree. Row layout honours the pack
  params (alignment, WebGL2 PACK_ROW_LENGTH/SKIP_PIXELS/SKIP_ROWS); script
  coordinates are widened to int64 before use. App framebuffers (GPU
  picking) and PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER reads stay exact. Shared by WebGL2 and
  OffscreenCanvas/worker contexts.
- New --fingerprint-webgl-readpixels-noise switch fed from
  noise.webgl_readpixels (default on).

Engine Fix Notes A2: audio noise was applied at read time inside
AudioBuffer::getChannelData, so getChannelData != copyFromChannel and
script-written buffers (CreepJS "trap") were perturbed. The amplitude
was a hard-coded 1e-5; audio_amplitude only toggled it.
- Remove read-time noise from AudioBuffer (and noised_channel_mask_).
- OfflineAudioContext::FireCompletionEvent perturbs the rendered buffer
  once, in place, before oncomplete fires and the promise resolves.
- --fingerprint-audio-noise now carries the amplitude;
  FingerprintState::SetAudioNoiseAmplitude clamps it to [0, 1e-2].
- AnalyserNode readouts scale with the amplitude, are off at 0, and
  leave silence (-Inf dB bins, 0/128/255 bytes, 0.0 samples) untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
